A04s (Metal track M6b boot 8): Panfrost's preprocessing, cached, and the preprocessed NIR kept only serialized.

panfrost_create_shader_state runs pan_shader_preprocess (the optimisation loop and the I/O lowering) on every
shader, and only then asks the disk cache for the compiled default variant, so a hit skips the backend but not
the preprocessing. backboardd on the A04s makes a pipeline for each of CoreAnimation's fixed_frag_lph_cph
specialisations (about forty in its first minutes of use); with every cache warm each still spent about 0.4 s of
CPU, on the thread that commits CoreAnimation's frames, against 0.02 s for its small shaders (M6b boot 7). Each
also kept the preprocessed NIR of both stages for the pipeline's life: about 2 MB of malloc per pipeline, for
variants the disk cache almost always has.

Keyed on so->nir_sha1 (the hash of the NIR as given, which the disk cache's binary keys already use) and the GPU,
the disk cache now also keeps the preprocessed NIR, serialized, with its shader_info, noperspective_varyings and
fragcolor_lowered. A shader found there is not preprocessed: so->nir becomes an empty shell with that
shader_info (all this driver reads of it after creation) and the serialization is kept as bytes. A shader not
found is preprocessed as before and then stored and kept the same way. panfrost_shader_get reads the bytes back
into NIR only to compile a variant the disk cache does not have.

Compiled binaries do not change: they come from the same preprocessed NIR, read back from its serialization, and
are stored under the same keys (check.sh compares the job chains, shaders included, with and without the
patch). That is why build-mesa-ios.sh leaves this file out of Panfrost's cache identity: the phone's cache stays
warm. Its entries carry their own tag (A04S_PRE_TAG), raised when their layout changes. Transform feedback keeps
the old path. A04S_PAN_PRE=0 turns it off; A04S_PAN_PRE_LOG=1 writes a line per shader to stderr;
a04s_panfrost_pre_counts() reports hits, stores, read-backs and the bytes kept. Mesa 25.0.7. Ours, under Mesa's
licence for the files it changes (MIT).

